    "problem": "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y =-x + 1$.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td>$0$</td>\n<td>$1$</td>\n<td>$2$</td>\n<td>$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n",
    "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=0,1,2,3$ into $y=-x+1$ gives $y=1,0,-1,-2$. The required graph passes through these four points and slopes downward.",
